<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prove Proposition <a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminaries ‣ Quantitative Approximation Rates for Group Equivariant Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#S2" title="2 Preliminaries ‣ Quantitative Approximation Rates for Group Equivariant Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first consider the case of <span id="A1.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">permutations</span>. Let <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/G\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}/S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/G\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}/S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is a compact set. The function</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex152" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F([X])=\|X\|_{F}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F([X])=\|X\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">is Lipschitz on <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> invariant, and therefore it is also Lipschitz
on the quotient space by Lemma <a href="#S5" title="5 Bi-Lipschitz invariant models ‣ Quantitative Approximation Rates for Group Equivariant Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. Therefore, it attains a maximum <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/G</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly, <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/G</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(B_{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(B_{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex153" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{M}=\{X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}|\quad\|X\|_{F}\leq M\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{M}=\{X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}|\quad\|X\|_{F}\leq M\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">For an appropriate <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=C(M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=C(M)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex154" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{r}(B_{M})\leq C_{M}r^{-nd},\quad\forall r&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{r}(B_{M})\leq C_{M}r^{-nd},\quad\forall r&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">and since the quotient map <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is 1-Lipschitz, we can push any cover of <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> of balls with radius <math id="A1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> to a cover of <math id="A1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(B_{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(B_{M})</annotation></semantics></math> by balls with the same radius. Thus</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex155" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{r}(K/G)\leq N_{r}(B_{M}/G)\leq N_{r}(B_{M})\leq C_{M}r^{-nd},\quad\forall r&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{r}(K/G)\leq N_{r}(B_{M}/G)\leq N_{r}(B_{M})\leq C_{M}r^{-nd},\quad\forall r&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next we consider the combined action of <span id="A1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">permutations and rigid motions</span>. Let <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> invariant set such that <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/G</annotation></semantics></math> is compact. As in (<a href="#S4.E87" title="Equation 87 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.2 Approximation rates for rotation invariant function spaces using frames ‣ 4 Approximation Rates for Functions Invariant to Permutations and Rigid Motions ‣ Quantitative Approximation Rates for Group Equivariant Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">87</span></a>), we denote</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex156" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{cent}(X)=X-\frac{1}{n}X1_{n}1_{n}^{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cent</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{cent}(X)=X-\frac{1}{n}X1_{n}1_{n}^{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The function <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F([X])=\|\mathrm{cent}(X)\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>cent</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F([X])=\|\mathrm{cent}(X)\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz on <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> and is <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> invariant. Therefore it is well defined and Lipschitz on the quotient space, by Lemma <a href="#S5" title="5 Bi-Lipschitz invariant models ‣ Quantitative Approximation Rates for Group Equivariant Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and therefore it attains a maximum <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/G</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/G</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="A1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(B_{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(B_{M})</annotation></semantics></math>. Next, we claim that <math id="A1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}/G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}/G</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="A1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex157" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\{X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}|X1_{n}=0_{d},X[i,j]=0,\forall d\geq i&gt;j\geq 1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\{X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}|X1_{n}=0_{d},X[i,j]=0,\forall d\geq i&gt;j\geq 1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">This is because, given any <math id="A1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> we can (a) centralize <math id="A1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, and then, denoting by <math id="A1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> the rank of <math id="A1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{cent}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cent</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{cent}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> (b) relabel the entries of <math id="A1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{X}=\mathrm{cent}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cent</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{X}=\mathrm{cent}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rank}(\tilde{x}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{x}_{k})=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rank}(\tilde{x}_{1},\ldots,\tilde{x}_{k})=k</annotation></semantics></math>. We can then apply the Gram-Schmidt procedure to obtain a rotation <math id="A1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\tilde{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\tilde{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is in <math id="A1.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> (if <math id="A1.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;d</annotation></semantics></math> this rotation still exists, but is not unique), and <math id="A1.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\tilde{X}\in[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\tilde{X}\in[X]</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that <math id="A1.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K/G\subseteq q(B_{M}\cap\mathcal{M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K/G\subseteq q(B_{M}\cap\mathcal{M})</annotation></semantics></math>
Under our assumption that <math id="A1.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq d+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq d+1</annotation></semantics></math>, the dimension of the subspace <math id="A1.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex158" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dim(\mathcal{M})=nd-\frac{d(d-1)}{2}-d=nd-\dim(E(d))=nd-\dim(G)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dim(\mathcal{M})=nd-\frac{d(d-1)}{2}-d=nd-\dim(E(d))=nd-\dim(G),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore there exists some <math id="A1.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex159" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{r}(B_{M}\cap\mathcal{M})\leq Cr^{-(nd-\dim(G))},\quad\forall r&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{r}(B_{M}\cap\mathcal{M})\leq Cr^{-(nd-\dim(G))},\quad\forall r&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Again using the fact that <math id="A1.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex160" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{r}(K/G)\leq N_{r}(q(B_{M}\cap\mathcal{M}))\leq N_{r}(B_{M}\cap\mathcal{M})\leq Cr^{-(nd-\dim(G))},\quad\forall r&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">dim</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{r}(K/G)\leq N_{r}(q(B_{M}\cap\mathcal{M}))\leq N_{r}(B_{M}\cap\mathcal{M})\leq Cr^{-(nd-\dim(G))},\quad\forall r&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
